      "text_unit_id": "tu_0008",
      "verbatim_text": "CRT may be a therapeutic option in ACHD patients with HF, but evidence in this specific setting is still lacking. Efficacy of CRT will depend on the underlying structural and functional substrate, such as anatomy of the systemic ventricle (left, right, or functionally single), presence and degree of structural systemic AV valve regurgitation, primary myocardial disease or scarring, and type of electrical conduction delay. 988"
